.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KINSPECT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kinspect
.Nd watch two virtual machines or pods, and the traffic between them, in one tmux window
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar vm1 vm2
.Nm
.Fl -pod Ar namespace Ns / Ns Ar pod1 namespace Ns / Ns Ar pod2
.Nm
.Fl -ip Ar address1 address2
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
finds the two endpoints' addresses \(em libvirt domains through
.Xr kldload-vm-ip 8 ,
pods through
.Xr kubectl 1 ,
or as given \(em and opens a window named
.Ql inspect
in the tmux session the web console's terminal drawer uses, replacing
any window of that name.
The window has three panes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It The flows, across the top
.Ql hubble observe
for the two addresses when the cluster runs Cilium; otherwise
.Xr tcpdump 8
on
.Ql virbr0 ,
through
.Xr sudo 8 .
.It One pane per endpoint, below
Established TCP sessions, link counters, load and the busiest processes,
refreshed every second, run on the endpoint itself: over ssh as root for
a machine or an address, through
.Ql kubectl exec
for a pod.
A pane that cannot reach its endpoint says so.
.El
.Pp
The addresses are typed into the panes' shells, so anything that does
not look like an address is refused.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -pod
The two arguments are pods, as
.Ar namespace Ns / Ns Ar pod .
.It Fl -ip
The two arguments are addresses; nothing is looked up.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0; so does no argument at all.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TMUX_SESSION
The tmux session; default
.Ql kldload .
.It Ev SSH_KEY
The key for the endpoints; default
.Pa /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 .
.It Ev LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI
Default
.Ql qemu:///system ,
whoever runs it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
The window is open.
.It 1
An endpoint has no address, or what it resolved to is not one.
.It 2
Not two endpoints.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Typical use, from the terminal drawer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kinspect web01 db01
# kinspect --pod shop/api-7d9f shop/postgres-0
.Ed
.Pp
What it refuses, on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30 with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kinspect web01
kinspect: need two vms (got 1)
# (exited 2)
$ kinspect no-such-vm other-vm
kinspect: could not resolve no-such-vm to an IP
# (exited 1)
$ kinspect --ip 10.0.0.5 '10.0.0.6;id'
kinspect: not an IP address: 10.0.0.6;id
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kubectl 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1 ,
.Xr kldload-session 8 ,
.Xr kldload-vm-ip 8 ,
.Xr tcpdump 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page, against a container running
.Xr sshd 8 :
the two endpoint panes ran on the host, not the endpoints, and showed
the host's own sessions and processes under the endpoints' names; kldload's
tmux configuration numbers panes from 1, so the flows pane was never
made; and
.Fl -pod
never found a pod, the namespace and name coming out empty.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The endpoint panes need ssh as root with
.Ev SSH_KEY ,
which only root can read, and host keys are not checked, since clones
get new ones.
.Pp
.Xr tcpdump 8
sees only what crosses
.Ql virbr0 ,
libvirt's default network; machines on another bridge show nothing
there.
